      "side": 1,
      "message": "All the hash fields are already sufficiently sized for SHA 512. And the open dice profile spec is very specific about the sice of these fields. So not only would the API need to change, the canonical formats would also change.\n\nThe spec is not so clear on the CDI secrets, though. libopen-dice uses fixed size arrays of size 32 bytes.\n\nMaybe Andrew or Darren can comment on this choice.",
